  "labels": {
    "anya": "Макс",
    "vika": "Вика",
    "lyova": "Лёва"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the kitchen of restaurant Victor, Max greets Vika and asks whether she knows the sex of their baby yet. When Vika coldly tells him she owes him nothing because he always lies, Max vows in front of the entire staff to speak only the truth.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, малыш!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы же знаете, кто у вас будет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Нет. Прекрати!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А почему я не знаю?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты должна мне сказать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Я ничего тебе не должна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Продолжай жить, как раньше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я изменился, я сейчас это докажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Кухня, внимание!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С этого момента прекращаю врать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И буду говорить только правду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Быстро за работу, Лавров!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Ты морковь нарезал?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, малыш!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, little one!' Notice how Russian expresses 'hello' and 'kid' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы же знаете, кто у вас будет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you know who you are having?' The meaning hinges on 'you' working together with 'will be' in spoken Russian. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Нет. Прекрати!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No. Stop it!' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'no' before landing on 'stop it'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А почему я не знаю?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And why do I not know?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'know'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты должна мне сказать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have to tell me.' Max addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'to say'. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Я ничего тебе не должна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not owe you anything.' Vika brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'nothing' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Продолжай жить, как раньше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Keep living just like before.' In Russian, the idea of 'continue' flows naturally into 'earlier' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я изменился, я сейчас это докажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have changed, I will prove it right now.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'will prove'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Кухня, внимание!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Kitchen, attention!' Notice how Russian expresses 'cuisine' and 'attention' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С этого момента прекращаю врать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'From this moment I stop lying.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'with' before landing on 'to lie'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И буду говорить только правду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I will speak only the truth.' Max brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'will be' in a few short words. Lyova answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Быстро за работу, Лавров!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quickly back to work, Lavrov!' Lyova anchors the line on 'quickly', while 'proper name' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Ты морковь нарезал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you chop the carrots?' The meaning hinges on 'you' working together with 'sliced' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
